 void Xteink::on_powerdown() {
+  // Light sleep and deep sleep share one global esp_sleep config, and light sleep
+  // leaves its wake sources armed. Deep sleep then inherits them and returns within
+  // milliseconds, waking and sleeping forever (measured: wakeup cause TIMER, then
+  // GPIO once the timer was cleared; reset reason DEEPSLEEP both times).
+  //   - TIMER: armed by every tickless-idle nap (CONFIG_PM_ENABLE), a few ms out.
+  //   - GPIO:  armed once by a touch-to-wake IRQ, and the touch rail is switched
+  //            off below, so the controller can no longer hold its INT line high.
+  // Deep sleep has its own wakeup_pin, so neither is ever wanted here. This runs
+  // from run_powerdown_hooks(), after teardown and immediately before
+  // esp_deep_sleep_start(), so no further nap can re-arm them.
+  esp_sleep_disable_wakeup_source(ESP_SLEEP_WAKEUP_TIMER);
+  esp_sleep_disable_wakeup_source(ESP_SLEEP_WAKEUP_GPIO);
   // Park the panel: booster off + DSLP. The SDK now skips the power-off sequence
   // when the screen is already off (re-issuing it after a full refresh hung on
   // BUSY and tripped the 5 s task watchdog, rebooting instead of sleeping). Feed
